  "description": "Shop-assembled shell boiler with the burner firing into a large furnace tube and hot gas making two to four passes through tubes surrounded by boiler water; the standard packaged steam source for small and medium gas-fired industrial loads. Wet-back reversal chambers give more heating surface than refractory-lined dry-back designs. Primary source: https://spiraxsarco.com/learn-about-steam/the-boiler-house/shell-boilers?sc_lang=en-GB",
